title: War Aims
card-image: img/cards/foreign_policy.svg?v=2
subtitle: Peace without annexations, the Stockholm conference and the offensive.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: coalition_affairs
view-if: foreign_policy_timer <= 0 and at_war = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; foreign_policy_timer = 3

The Allies want the offensive. The soldiers want peace. The Soviet's formula is peace without annexations or indemnities, but nobody has agreed to negotiate on it.

- @note: Send a new note to the Allies on war aims.
- @stockholm: Back the Stockholm conference of the International.
- @offensive: Prepare the offensive with the Allies.
- @separate: Sound out Germany through neutral intermediaries.
- @easy_discard

@note

How should the party go about it? Cautiously, with compromises, it will cost a resource, do less and anger less. In full, it will do all that it says, and its opponents will answer. And a party strong enough can carry it out and break its opponents.

- @note_slow: Go about it cautiously, with compromises.
- @note_decree: Carry it out in full.
- @note_force: Carry it out in full, and break any opposition by force.

@note_slow
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: Milder effects and little anger. Costs 1 resource.
unavailable-subtitle: We have nothing to pay the compensation with.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'slow', () => {
RO.add(Q, {war_weariness: -2, rel_kad: -2});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 2, workers: 1});
Q.war_aims_note = 1;
}, "Send a new note to the Allies on war aims");
!}

A note on war aims went to London and Paris. They replied politely, and not at all. (It was done cautiously, with compromises.)



@note_decree
subtitle: All that it says. Its opponents will answer.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'decree', () => {
RO.add(Q, {war_weariness: -2, rel_kad: -2});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 2, workers: 1});
Q.war_aims_note = 1;
}, "Send a new note to the Allies on war aims");
!}

A note on war aims went to London and Paris. They replied politely, and not at all.



@note_force
view-if: bol_regime = 0
choose-if: strength >= 18
subtitle: Your chance of breaking each camp it angers: Kadets [+ odds_kad +]%. Any camp under 45% is too strong for you, and is left alone.
unavailable-subtitle: We lack the force and the allies to break the opposition.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'force', () => {
RO.add(Q, {war_weariness: -2, rel_kad: -2});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 2, workers: 1});
Q.war_aims_note = 1;
}, "Send a new note to the Allies on war aims");
!}

A note on war aims went to London and Paris. They replied politely, and not at all. [+ law_text +]

@stockholm

How should the party go about it? Cautiously, with compromises, it will cost a resource, do less and anger less. In full, it will do all that it says, and its opponents will answer. And a party strong enough can carry it out and break its opponents.

- @stockholm_slow: Go about it cautiously, with compromises.
- @stockholm_decree: Carry it out in full.
- @stockholm_force: Carry it out in full, and break any opposition by force.

@stockholm_slow
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: Milder effects and little anger. Costs 1 resource.
unavailable-subtitle: We have nothing to pay the compensation with.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'slow', () => {
Q.stockholm = (Q.stockholm || 0) + 1;
RO.add(Q, {war_weariness: -4, rel_kad: -4, army_discipline: -1});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 3, workers: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 2, -2);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 4);
}, "Back the Stockholm conference of the International");
!}

The government has officially endorsed a socialist conference at Stockholm. The Allied governments refuse passports to their own socialists. [? if stockholm >= 3 : Delegates from four neutral and enemy countries are on their way. ?] (It was done cautiously, with compromises.)



