@offensive
on-arrival: {!
Q.offensive_prepared = 1;
RO.add(Q, {war_weariness: 3, army_discipline: 3, rel_kad: 4});
RO.boost(Q, {middle: 3, soldiers: -3});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 2, 0);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 4);
!}

Kerensky is visiting the front, and the Soviet has given its blessing. The army is getting ready for an offensive that it does not want.

@separate
choose-if: stockholm >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: We must first have shown our commitment to a general peace at Stockholm.

How should the party go about it? Cautiously, with compromises, it will cost a resource, do less and anger less. In full, it will do all that it says, and its opponents will answer. And a party strong enough can carry it out and break its opponents.

- @separate_slow: Go about it cautiously, with compromises.
- @separate_decree: Carry it out in full.
- @separate_force: Carry it out in full, and break any opposition by force.

@separate_slow
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: Milder effects and little anger. Costs 1 resource.
unavailable-subtitle: We have nothing to pay the compensation with.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'slow', () => {
Q.separate_feelers = 1;
RO.add(Q, {war_weariness: -6, rel_kad: -6, right_threat: 3});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 3});
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', -2, 6);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, -1);
}, "Sound out Germany through neutral intermediaries");
!}

An unofficial approach, through a Swedish socialist, asked if Germany would consider terms on the basis of no annexations. The answer was not hostile. The Kadets learned of it and are furious. (It was done cautiously, with compromises.)



